{"id": "EUVD-2026-104300", "enisaUuid": "a36387fd-2640-32fb-a95b-9e70bddefc79", "description": "libtins through 4.6 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in DNS::compose_name in src/dns.cpp that allows remote attackers to read past the packet buffer by sending a label ending exactly at the packet end. Attackers can deliver crafted DNS packets whose additional, answer, or authority records trigger a one-byte read when parsed, crashing applications on hardened allocators.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T02:51:25", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libtins-dns-name-parsing-oob-read", "https://github.com/mfontanini/libtins/blob/v4.6/src/dns.cpp#L338-L389", "https://github.com/mfontanini/libtins", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libtins-through-4.6-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-dns-compose-name"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q9cp-6gg7-9cpm", "CVE-2026-112273"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f443bab1-1220-31ec-8824-dc5033e5cb18", "product": {"name": "libtins", "vendor": {"name": "libtins"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1d118a66-12df-33c6-bad3-0023f4173e7e", "vendor": {"name": "libtins"}}], "isExploited": false}